 "season_definition": "The fire season has ended on the first day after its peak from which the 7-day running count (centred) of NASA FIRMS MODIS active-fire detections (Terra + Aqua, Collection 6.1, 'presumed vegetation fire' type) inside 4S-0, 110-117E -- the Central/South Kalimantan peat belt used by Field et al. (2016, PNAS) -- stays below 10% of that season's highest 7-day count for 14 consecutive days. The end date is the first of those 14 days, so it can only be confirmed 17 days later. A season starts on the first day after 1 May on which the count exceeds 10% of the maximum and stays above it for 7 days. A year whose maximum is below the 10th percentile of all years' maxima (2001-2025) has no season. This is this site's own definition [engineering judgement]; no published definition of fire-season end exists.",
