 "caveats": [
  "About 22 fitted seasons and seven coefficients: enough to fit, barely enough to validate. Judge the model by the leave-one-out and forecast-mode errors.",
  "The season labels are this site's own rule on MODIS fire counts. A different threshold (5% or 20% of the season maximum; 7 or 21 quiet days) moves end dates by days to weeks, and the coefficients move with them.",
  "MODIS Terra/Aqua orbits have drifted since about 2020-2022, changing overpass times and fire counts. Relative thresholds absorb a constant change, not a trend within a season.",
  "The rainfall generator's climatology includes the season being forecast (it is fitted on 1981-2025), a small leak that flatters forecast-mode error slightly.",
  "Parameter uncertainty is not propagated into the published interval; the p10-p90 band is weather uncertainty only.",
  "Land use changed across 2001-2025 (drainage, the 2011 moratorium, the 2016 peat restoration agency); one stationary coefficient set papers over that."
 ],
